Azure RBAC role assignments target a security principal's Microsoft Entra service principal, which is available regardless of region, so Managed1, Managed2, and the system-assigned identities of VM1 and VM2 can all receive the Owner role at the RG1 scope. VM3 has no system-assigned identity of its own -- it only uses the attached user-assigned identity Managed1, which is already the principal that receives the role -- so VM3 cannot itself be selected as a separate principal, and VM4 has no identity at all. For the same reason a user-assigned managed identity's service principal is region-independent, Managed2 (West US) can be attached to a virtual machine in any region, so VM1, VM2, VM3, and VM4 can all be assigned Managed2.
----------
AZURE RBAC & MANAGED IDENTITIES ARCHITECTURE

├── SECURITY PRINCIPALS & REGIONAL SCOPE
│   ├── Microsoft Entra Service Principals
│   │   ├── Region-independent (Global scope across Entra ID)
│   │   └── Direct RBAC Target (Roles attach to Principals, not directly to VM objects)
│   │
│   └── Regional Flexibility
│       ├── User-Assigned Identities (e.g., Managed2 in West US)
│       └── Cross-Region Attachment (Can be attached to VMs in any Azure region)

├── RG1 ROLE ASSIGNMENT SCOPE: "OWNER" ROLE
│   ├── Eligible Principals (Can receive Owner role)
│   │   ├── Managed1 (User-assigned Managed Identity)
│   │   ├── Managed2 (User-assigned Managed Identity)
│   │   ├── VM1 System-Assigned Identity
│   │   └── VM2 System-Assigned Identity
│   │
│   └── Ineligible VMs (Cannot receive Owner role directly)
│       ├── VM3 
│       │   └── Reason: No System-Assigned ID (Uses Managed1; identity is already covered)
│       └── VM4 
│           └── Reason: No identity enabled at all

└── VM ATTACHMENT PERMISSIONS: ATTACHING "MANAGED2"
    ├── Attachment Capability
    │   └── Applicable to ALL target virtual machines regardless of location
    │
    └── VM Attachment Matrix
        ├── VM1 ──► Can attach Managed2
        ├── VM2 ──► Can attach Managed2
        ├── VM3 ──► Can attach Managed2
        └── VM4 ──► Can attach Managed2
Key Takeaways
Core Principle: Azure RBAC targets Entra ID Service Principals, which are global entities independent of Azure regions.

Role Delegation: Role assignments are bound to the identity (Managed1, Managed2, VM1/VM2 System IDs), not to the physical VM resource itself.

Identity Mobility: User-Assigned Identities (like Managed2) can be associated with resources residing in any region.
